\section{Persistent controls}{

\code{\link[=set_control_computation]{set_control_computation()}} sets \code{seed}, \code{ncores}, and \code{strategy} for the
session, and each call of \code{control_mrqap()} then uses them where they are
not given. A control given in the call takes priority, then one from
\code{\link[=control_computation]{control_computation()}}, then the option, then the default.
\code{control_mrqap()} marks each control that comes from an option with
\code{(option)}. It reads the options when it is called, so its result keeps
the same controls if the options change later.

\code{persist = TRUE} is deprecated, and warns once in a session.
It still writes the computation controls that it is given with
\code{\link[=set_control_computation]{set_control_computation()}}, and the other controls to
\code{options(infernet.control)}. That option is read until infernet 0.8.0,
and a computation control in \code{options(snet_computation)} takes priority
over it. \code{persist = FALSE} clears both options.

Every result records the controls that it used, as \code{control} (an
attribute of a \code{diffs_model}). Give that record as \code{control} to fit the
same model again without the options of the session.
